      en: "Sar-e-Sang is a mining site in Badakhshan province, northeastern Afghanistan, at an elevation of about 2,800 meters in the Kokcha Valley. It is famous for its lapis lazuli mines, among the oldest in the world. The mines produce high-quality lapis lazuli, which has been mined for millennia. The economy of the area is heavily dependent on mining. The population is predominantly Tajik. Infrastructure is basic, with mining conducted using traditional methods. Sar-e-Sang holds great historical significance for lapis lazuli trade routes.",
